  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Centralize disposal in PooledObject:\n      - Move IDisposable implementation to the PooledObject base class and remove duplicate Dispose implementations from pooled types.\n      - PooledObject now implements IDisposable, exposes a protected virtual Dispose(bool) for derived cleanup, and calls Lucifer.Return(this) + GC.SuppressFinalize(this).\n      - Removed explicit IDisposable declarations and Dispose methods from HttpModel, PacketModel, WsModel, Buffer, and Utf8Builder, and added small inline/annotation tweaks (e.g. ThrowDisposedException inlined and LuciferCore.Main using).\n      - This consolidates pool return logic and reduces repeated code across pooled objects.\n      Dispose pooled objects instead of Lucifer.Return:\n      - Replace many direct Lucifer.Return(...) calls with explicit Dispose() calls on pooled buffers/objects to centralize resource cleanup and clarify lifetimes.\n      - Changes touch SimulationManager, HttpModel, PacketModel, WsModel, WsSessionProtocol, ServerTransport, SessionTransport, CacheService, RateLimitService, SessionService, Utf8Builder and others.\n      - PooledObject.Dispose no longer invokes a protected Dispose(bool) hook (the virtual Dispose(bool) was removed) and now returns the object to the pool.",
